{
  "date": "2026-10-25",
  "scope": "Actual reader-root registration/extension and ordered release, completion submission-before-commit updates and producer continuation called by Coordinator::apply. Complete event dispatch, root extraction, history composition and worker-retirement retain/callback refinement remain open.",
  "properties": {
    "queue_reader::{identity,contains,create,extend}": "Exact attempt extraction; native Value-equality search; lease/root construction; root extension preserves all earlier roots and the existing lease, includes a new input, avoids duplicate native-equal inputs and rejects malformed entries without mutation.",
    "queue_reader::{register,progress,remove}": "Actual selected-attempt updates, exact local success/error classification, no-mutation local errors and preservation of peer entries. Register replaces its selected attempt as before; attempt freshness is a separate admission obligation.",
    "queue_reader::{done,extension_preserves_all_roots,matches_worker}": "Ordered ReaderDone execution removes precisely the specified attempts, admits repeated IDs and describes the exact processed prefix before an invalid identity. The extension theorem preserves each prior root by position. Worker matching is the actual predicate; the enclosing native Map::retain operation is not proved.",
    "queue_receipt::{submission,record}": "Exact receipt/lease object, selected submission update before receipt append, preservation of every preceding commit and unrelated state, and exact partial submission prefix if the commit list is invalid. Missing submission identity is rejected before edits. A correctly shaped state/event cannot be rejected arbitrarily.",
    "queue_receipt::continue_producer": "Change only the selected producer continuation, preserving its JSON content/observations and all peer entries. Missing/nonstring producer ID is a no-op, matching the existing dispatcher; an invalid selected table is rejected unchanged."
  },
  "runtime_changes": "Coordinator delegates these existing in-memory mutations to verified bodies. Root deduplication uses an explicit ordered loop with the same native Value equality and no extra collection; registration/progress/removal retain their selected-entry semantics. Invalid internal record shapes now produce defined recovery errors. No new filesystem operation or persisted-format change. No newly demonstrated valid-API bug or measured zero-overhead claim.",
  "boundaries": [
    "ENV-JSON-LIBRARY newly trusts only <Value as PartialEq>::eq. Its result follows an opaque native equality relation; true results preserve all finite-depth observations. It does not imply equal serialized bytes or representation identity: floating positive/negative zero can compare equal. Numeric observations remain as_u64-only.",
    "The runner rejects preserve_order and requires float_roundtrip on the actual locked dependency artifact. Equality of ordered object observations relies on the pinned sorted-map configuration. There are twenty audited primitive methods, four opaque types and the existing two named Value library laws; no executable straw body is admitted.",
    "Reader registration can replace an existing selected attempt, as in the prior implementation. Correct fresh attempt/lease dispatch is a caller obligation. Cancellation/expiration/epoch preservation is covered by native integration tests; a complete Coordinator event-dispatch proof is still absent.",
    "The matches_worker predicate is verified; native serde Map::retain and its callback composition for ReaderRetired are still outside the actual-body proof. External acknowledgement/fencing must establish that retired readers have stopped.",
    "Local helper errors do not imply whole-event rollback. Earlier task/cache/reader mutations may already have happened; commit quarantine and failed-constructor behavior remain native caller obligations. Receipt errors explicitly expose the completed submission prefix.",
    "Complete root extraction, ownership correspondence, request/lease admission, derived caches, queue history refinement, native WAL/run/File/lock binding and cross-log/GC composition remain unfinished. These results do not close the corresponding broad verification obligations or prove automatic model-checkpoint selection."
  ],
